course: dictionary
lesson: 7357
title: Playmate
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A playmate is a friend that a child plays with. You can work out the meaning from the word itself: play, and mate, which means friend. Read the context: «Only children often learn to make friends fast, because they want a playmate.» They want someone to play with, so a playmate is that someone.
explain: Playmate is a noun, so it can change to playmates when there is more than one. Phrases help too: «a childhood playmate» is a friend you played with when you were very young, and «a new playmate» is someone who has just started to play with you.
explain: Playmate is used about young children, but it can also be used about animals that play together, like two puppies. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence: "because they want a friend to play with" still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: A playmate is a friend that a child plays with.
fact: Playmate is a noun: one playmate, and more than one playmates.
fact: «Playmate» is made from two words: play and mate, and a mate is a friend.
fact: Animals can be playmates too, when they play together.
fact: «A childhood playmate» is a friend you played with when you were very young.
exercise: «Only children often learn to make friends fast, because they want a playmate.» What is a playmate? | A place where children eat lunch | *A friend that a child plays with | A teacher who runs the playground | A toy that cannot move
exercise: Which two words make up playmate? | play and time | *play and mate | pay and mate | plays and mates
exercise: «A new playmate» means | a long walk to school | *a friend a child has just started to play with | a teacher who has just arrived | a new toy that makes a noise
test: Which word means a friend a child plays with? | teacher | neighbour | *playmate | parent
test: What is the plural of playmate? | *playmates | playmate's | playmateses | playmen
exam: Which best explains «a childhood playmate»? | A grown-up you work with | A toy you played with before breakfast | *A friend you played with when you were very young | A place where children learn to read
